		<title>Huawei tells customers to find their own AI chip memory, effectively outsourcing procurement to the black market</title>
		<link>https://the-decoder.com/huawei-tells-customers-to-find-their-own-ai-chip-memory-effectively-outsourcing-procurement-to-the-black-market/</link>
					<comments>https://the-decoder.com/huawei-tells-customers-to-find-their-own-ai-chip-memory-effectively-outsourcing-procurement-to-the-black-market/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Maximilian Schreiner]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 03 Nov 2026 11:47:37 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AI in practice]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Artificial Intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[China]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Huawei]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[USA]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=42335</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1456" height="816" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/china_ai_chip.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="An investigation by the New York Times shows that despite US export restrictions, there is a lively trade in advanced AI chips in China. Dozens of suppliers in Shenzhen are doing business worth over 100 million dollars in some cases." style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>        Huawei is telling customers to source the high-performance memory for its AI chips on their own, pushing them onto the black market. Smugglers are exploiting a loophole in U.S. export rules by bundling HBM with low-end processors, shipping them through Hong Kong, and separating the chips on site. Prices for smuggled HBM3E memory have surged to around $4,000 per unit in just one year.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/huawei-tells-customers-to-find-their-own-ai-chip-memory-effectively-outsourcing-procurement-to-the-black-market/">Huawei tells customers to find their own AI chip memory, effectively outsourcing procurement to the black market</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
